monitoring\",\n        \"taskIds\": [\n          4\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Document published dataset SLAs\",\n        \"taskIds\": [\n          5\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Create data dictionary & documentation for datasets and models\",\n        \"taskIds\": [\n          6\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Create end-user documentation & FAQ guides\",\n        \"taskIds\": [\n          7\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Create incident response & troubleshooting playbooks\",\n        \"taskIds\": [\n          8,\n          9\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Create user access request & onboarding workflow\",\n        \"taskIds\": [\n          10\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"rows\": [\n      [\n        \"\",\n        1,\n        \"Create Databricks Runbook (execution, restart logic, troubleshooting)\",\n        \"Yes\",\n        \"Copilot generates documentation\",\n        \"Databricks, Synapse, Fabric\",\n        \"Github Copilot\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"\",\n        2,\n        \"Create data contract for all published datasets (schema, SLAs, DQ rules, lineage)\",\n        \"Yes\",\n        \"Copilot generates templates\",\n        \"\",\n        \"GitHub Copilot\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"\",\n        3,\n        \"Create lineage documentation for each published dataset\",\n        \"Yes\",\n        \"Copilot generates documentation\",\n        \"Unity Catalog Lineage, Fabric Lineage View\",\n        \"GitHub Copilot\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"\",\n        4,\n        \"Ensure compatibility for downstream semantic model consumption (Power BI)\",\n        \"Partial\",\n        \"Copilot suggests checks\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"\",\n        5,\n        \"Document published dataset SLAs (availability, freshness, latency)\",\n        \"Yes\",\n        \"Copilot generates documentation\",\n        \"Azure DevOps Wiki\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"\",\n        6,\n        \"Document data dictionary for all datasets and semantic models\",\n        \"Yes\",\n        \"Copilot can extract metadata and generate comprehensive data dictionaries with descriptions, types, and business definitions\",\n        \"Power BI, Tabular, OneNote, Azure DevOps\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"\",\n        7,\n        \"Create FAQ documentation for end users\",\n        \"Partial\",\n        \"Copilot can structure and generate FAQ templates, but actual questions/answers require real user feedback\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"\",\n        8,\n        \"Create incident response playbooks\",\n        \"Yes\",\n        \"Copilot can generate incident classification, escalation procedure and resolution workflow.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"Github Copilot\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"\",\n        9,\n        \"Create semantic model refresh troubleshooting guide\",\n        \"Yes\",\n        \"Copilot can generate Power BI refresh error codes, causes, and resolution steps\",\n        \"Power BI, Tabular model\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"\",\n        10,\n        \"Create user access request workflow\",\n        \"Yes\",\n        \"Copilot can generate access request forms, approval workflows, and provisioning scripts\",\n        \"Powerapps, Azure DevOps, Databricks, Fabric, Syanpse\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ]\n    ]\n  },\n  \"109\": {\n    \"title\": \"Agile Process\",\n    \"columns\": [\n      \"Category\",\n      \"Task\",\n      \"Purpose\",\n      \"Can it be Automated?\",\n      \"Comments\"\n    ],\n    \"userStories\": [],\n    \"rows\": [\n      [\n        \"Backlog Grooming\",\n        \"Create user stories with clearly defined acceptance criteria to ensure alignment on expected outcomes\",\n        \"Ensure alignment on expected outcomes. Everyone knows exactly what \\\"done\\\" looks like before work begins\",\n        \"Partial\",\n        \"Copilot can suggest story templates, phrasing, or examples, but context-specific input is required.\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Backlog Grooming\",\n        \"Review and prioritize the product backlog to decide which features to be prioritized\",\n        \"Decide which features deliver the highest business value. Team always works on what matters most.\",\n        \"No\",\n        \"Requires business understanding and stakeholder decision-making.\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Retrospective\",\n        \"Conduct a bi-weekly sprint retrospective to identify what went well, what needs improvement, and actionable next steps\",\n        \"Reflect on the sprint to identify what went well, what didn't, and how the team can improve\",\n        \"No\",\n        \"Requires Tean discussion\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Sprint Planning\",\n        \"Estimate effort for each task using story points or hours to support realistic sprint planning and capacity allocation\",\n        \"Support realistic sprint planning and capacity allocation. Team commits only to what it can actually deliver\",\n        \"No\",\n        \"Business understanding and complexity analysis required\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Daily Standup\",\n        \"Document key discussion points, decisions, and action items during huddles and share meeting notes promptly with the team\",\n        \"Capture key discussion points, decisions, and action items during huddles. Share meeting notes promptly after each session\",\n        \"Yes\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Daily Standup\",\n        \"Facilitate daily standup and evening huddle sessions to synchronize the team on progress, plans, and blockers\",\n        \"Round-robin: Done/Doing/Blocked. Synchronize the team on progress, plans, and blockers. PM escalates immediately\",\n        \"No\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Sprint Planning\",\n        \"Conduct bi-weekly sprint planning sessions to define the sprint scope, set priorities, and commit to deliverables\",\n        \"Capacity review, backlog grooming, story pointing, sprint goal. Define scope, set priorities, and commit to deliverables.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Sprint Planning\",\n        \"Define the Sprint Goal, a clear objective for the sprint\",\n        \"Set a clear, focused objective for the sprint. Gives the team one shared target to rally around.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Metrics\",\n        \"Measure and report team velocity at the end of each sprint to support future capacity planning and forecasting\",\n        \"Track story points delivered per sprint. Support future capacity planning and forecasting with data, not guesswork.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Sprint Review\",\n        \"Collect and document stakeholder feedback from sprint review and update backlogs accordingly\",\n        \"Capture input from sprint review and feed it back into the backlog. Stakeholder voice shapes what gets built next.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Metrics\",\n        \"Prepare and present MBR (monthly)\",\n        \"Give Business owners a clear monthly view of progress, risks, metrics, and outcomes.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Metrics\",\n        \"Prepare and present QBR (quarterly)\",\n        \"Assess long-term trajectory with stakeholders. Realign strategy, review KPIs, and plan ahead.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Daily Standup\",\n        \"Maintain daily task updates in ADO — including status changes, hours logged, and any blockers\",\n        \"Update status changes, hours logged, and blockers. Ensure task statuses reflect current state; no stale items.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Retrospective\",\n        \"Track and follow up on retrospective action items to ensure continuous improvement is carried forward into the next sprint\",\n        \"Ensure improvement actions are carried forward into the next sprint. They don't just get discussed — they get done.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Sprint Review\",\n        \"Maintain and update project documentation (wiki, runbooks, process docs)\",\n        \"Keep wiki, runbooks, and process docs current. Preserve knowledge so the team isn't dependent on any single person.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Sprint Review\",\n        \"Collaborate with the FA team to schedule and complete external reviews within the defined timeline\",\n        \"Schedule and complete external reviews within the defined timeline. Prevent reviews from becoming delivery blockers.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Sprint Review\",\n        \"Collect and document stakeholder feedback from sprint review and update backlogs accordingly\",\n        \"Capture stakeholder input post sprint review. Update backlog priorities accordingly to reflect new learnings.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Backlog Grooming\",\n        \"Identify and document dependencies between stories or with other teams early in planning\",\n        \"Map cross-story and cross-team dependencies upfront. Avoid surprises and last-minute bottlenecks.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Backlog Grooming\",\n        \"Conduct Backlog Grooming/Refinement sessions (mid-sprint) to keep upcoming stories ready\",\n        \"Clarify, split, and refine upcoming stories. Keep them sprint-ready so the next cycle starts without delays.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Sprint Review\",\n        \"Close the sprint formally — move incomplete items back to the backlog, update ADO status, and prepare for the next sprint cycle\",\n        \"Move incomplete items back to the backlog, update ADO status, and prepare for the next sprint cycle. Clean close every time.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Daily Standup\",\n        \"Maintain and update the sprint board in real time to provide visibility into task status (To Do → In Progress → Done)\",\n        \"Provide visibility into task status (To Do → In Progress → Done). Ensure the board reflects reality at all times.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Daily Standup\",\n        \"Identify, escalate, and resolve blockers promptly to keep the sprint on track and prevent delivery delays\",\n        \"Flag blockers in standup, escalate immediately, track to resolution. Keep the sprint on track and prevent delivery delays.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Backlog Grooming\",\n        \"Map Feature Dependencies across the Product Backlog\",\n        \"To identify technical or sequence-based blockers between different user stories early, ensuring the development team works on high-priority tasks in the correct order.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"Relationship Extraction: Analyzes natural language in user stories to automatically flag keywords (e.g., \\\"requires,\\\" \\\"depends on,\\\" \\\"after\\\") and suggest link types between tickets.\\r\\n\\r\\nSequence Optimization: Simulates different development paths to recommend the most efficient order of operations, preventing developers from starting a task only to find its prerequisite is missing\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Retrospective\",\n        \"Perform a Bottleneck and Blockage Root-Cause Analysis\",\n        \"To identify recurring friction points in the \\\"In Progress\\\" or \\\"Review\\\" stages of the board and implement structural changes to improve lead time.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"Analyzes pull request comments and ticket history to detect if bottlenecks are caused by technical complexity, unclear requirements, or personality-driven review friction.\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Metrics\",\n        \"Audit Automated Test Coverage per User Story\",\n        \"To verify that the ratio of automated unit/integration tests scales proportionally with new feature development, ensuring the \\\"Done\\\" state reflects true stability.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"Code-to-Story Mapping: Correlates new code lines in a PR with the specific User Story ID to verify if corresponding unit test files were created or modified.\\r\\n\\r\\nGap Identification: Scans the logic of a new feature and suggests missing test cases (e.g., edge cases or boundary values) that a developer might have overlooked\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Metrics\",\n        \"Profile Environment Stability and Deployment Readiness\",\n        \"To analyze the frequency of failures in Dev/Stage environments to identify infrastructure instability that prevents the team from reaching a \\\"shippable\\\" state at the end of the cycle.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"Log Clustering: Aggregates thousands of lines of deployment logs to identify the \\\"Signal in the Noise,\\\" pinpointing whether a failure was a transient network issue or a recurring configuration conflict.\\r\\n\\r\\nPredictive Alerting: Analyzes trends in Dev/Stage failures to predict a \\\"Deployment Red Zone\\\" before the team attempts a production release.\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"Backlog Grooming\",\n        \"Perform a Definition of Ready (DoR) Gap Analysis\",\n        \"To evaluate incoming user stories for missing technical requirements (e.g., lack of API specs or clear acceptance criteria) before they enter the sprint to reduce mid-sprint churn.\",\n        \"\",\n        \"Automated Gatekeeping: Acts as a pre-sprint filter by scanning user stories against a DoR checklist and flagging those missing critical artifacts like API contracts, UI mockups, or Acceptance Criteria.\\r\\n\\r\\nDrafting Support: If a story is flagged as \\\"Not Ready,\\\" the AI can automatically generate draft acceptance criteria or boilerplate API specs based on the story's title and description.\"\n      ]\n    ]\n  }\n}"
          },
